<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n58850" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κομψ-εύω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>refine upon</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόμψευέ νυν τὴν
				δόξαν</span> aye, <i>quibble on</i> the word <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόξα</span> (referring to the previous line),
				<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				324
			</span></i>:—mostly in 
				Med.
			, <i>to be smart, ingenious</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἥδεσθαι κομψευόμενος</span> to be fond <i>of clever
				inventions</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Art.</u>
				70
			</span></i> (glossed <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πανουργευόμενος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Erot.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ τοῦτο κομψευσάμενος</span>
			he who <i>invented</i> this <i>subtlety</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				489b
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρέπει . . σοφιστῇ τὰ τοιαῦτα
					κομψεύεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>La.</u>
					197d
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ὡς</span> . . <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>R.</u>
				436d
			</span></i>: pf.
			
				Pass.
			 in med. sense, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐτὸ τοῦτο καὶ
				κεκόμψευται</span> he <i>has advanced</i> this <i>dainty
				paradox</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				227c
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ τὰ πολιτικὰ κεκομψευμένοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.448
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, of things, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσαγώγιον
				κεκομψευμένον</span>
			<i>neatly made</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phlb.</u>
				56c
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ λόγος ὑπὸ τῶν τοιούτων κεκόμψευται
					σχημάτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					<u>Isoc.</u>
					14
				</span></i>
			.</div>
